  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Resettlement Programme with the Government of Denmark from Rwanda to Denmark under the 2021 Resettlement Quota &#x2013; Phase II</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UNHCR estimates that over 2 million refugees globally will be in need of resettlement by 2023. In view of the limited places available for resettlement, the most vulnerable with the greatest protection risks need to be prioritized. In this overall context, in June 2021 Denmark announced that it would resettle 200 beneficiaries from Rwanda to Denmark under the 2021 resettlement quota. The 2021 quota would primarily be female-headed households and their families, but also persons at risk of persecution due to sexual orientation. 
 
In this project, IOM is contributing to providing a durable solution to approximately 40 beneficiaries of international protection in Rwanda by facilitating their resettlement to Denmark. IOM aims to achieve the project&apos;s objective by working towards the following outcomes: Beneficiaries&apos; medical needs and public health concerns have been comprehensively addressed and can be followed up in the resettlement country; and Beneficiaries are able to travel in a safe, regular, and informed manner from their country of first asylum to their final destination in the resettlement country.</narrative>
  </description>
